  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "For two strings AAA and BBB with the same length NNN, we will say that they are equivalent if the following rule holds: For each pair of integers lll and rrr (1≤l≤r≤N1 \\le l \\le r \\le N1≤l≤r≤N), the substring of AAA between the lll-th and rrr-th character (inclusive) is a palindrome if and only if the substring of BBB between the lll-th and rrr-th character (inclusive) is a palindrome.\n\nYou are given a string SSS with length NNN. Find the number of sets P⊂{1,2,…,N}P \\subset \\{1, 2, \\ldots, N\\}P⊂{1,2,…,N} such that there is a character ccc and a string XXX which is equivalent to SSS and satisfies Xp=cX_p = cXp​=c for each p∈Pp \\in Pp∈P. Since the answer may be large, compute it modulo 998,244,353998,244,353998,244,353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1,0001 \\le T \\le 1,0001≤T≤1,000",
      "1≤N≤2,0001 \\le N \\le 2,0001≤N≤2,000",
      "SSS contains only lowercase Latin letters",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (10 points):** N≤10N \\le 10N≤10",
      "**Subtask #2 (90 points):** T≤10T \\le 10T≤10"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains a single string SSS with length NNN.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing one integer ― the number of subsets of characters that can be equal to each other in some string equivalent to SSS, modulo 998,244,353998,244,353998,244,353.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
